#### 10. String Concatenation in `GetProductImageURLOriginal` Allocates on Every Call

- **Category**: Object Creation & Memory
- **File**: `/Users/admin/project/legacy/searchapi-elastic/common/utils/utils.go:316-333`
- **Impact**: The current fallback function (which remains the fallback in the new design) performs 3-5 string concatenations per call using `+`, plus a `strconv.Atoi`, `math.Floor`, and `fmt.Sprintf` (line 328). Each concatenation allocates a new string. With 40 products per search and this function called for all PRODTYPE=="1" items (plus bundles), this is ~40-80 allocations per search request, producing short-lived garbage.

    This matters because the function is the fallback path. When the circuit breaker opens, ALL image URL resolution falls back to this function, making it the hot path during degraded mode.

- **Current Code** (Bad):
    ```go
    // utils.go:316-333
    func GetProductImageURLOriginal(productCode string) (imageURL string) {
        code, _ := strconv.Atoi(productCode)
        if code > 0 {
            if code > 500000 {
                subImagePath1 := productCode[len(productCode)-3 : len(productCode)]
                subImagePath2 := productCode[len(productCode)-6 : len(productCode)-3]
                // 5 concatenations = 4 intermediate strings
                imageURL = "http://img.danawa.com/prod_img/500000/" + subImagePath1 + "/" + subImagePath2 + "/img/" + productCode + "_1.jpg"
            } else {
                // fmt.Sprintf + math.Floor + concatenation
                imageURL = "http://img.danawa.com/prod_img/large/group_" + fmt.Sprintf("%.0f", math.Floor(float64(code)/500)) + "/" + productCode + "_1.jpg"
            }
        }
        return
    }
    ```

- **Suggested Fix** (Good):
    ```go
    func GetProductImageURLOriginal(productCode string) string {
        code, _ := strconv.Atoi(productCode)
        if code <= 0 {
            return ""
        }
        // Pre-sized builder avoids intermediate allocations
        var b strings.Builder
        b.Grow(80) // Typical URL length
        if code > 500000 {
            n := len(productCode)
            b.WriteString("http://img.danawa.com/prod_img/500000/")
            b.WriteString(productCode[n-3 : n])
            b.WriteByte('/')
            b.WriteString(productCode[n-6 : n-3])
            b.WriteString("/img/")
            b.WriteString(productCode)
            b.WriteString("_1.jpg")
        } else {
            b.WriteString("http://img.danawa.com/prod_img/large/group_")
            b.WriteString(strconv.Itoa(code / 500)) // Integer division, no float needed
            b.WriteByte('/')
            b.WriteString(productCode)
            b.WriteString("_1.jpg")
        }
        return b.String()
    }
    ```

- **Expected Improvement**: Reduces allocations per call from ~5 to 1 (single `b.String()` call). Eliminates `math.Floor` and `fmt.Sprintf` overhead on the else-branch. Under circuit-breaker-open conditions with ~1000 QPS and 40 products each, saves ~40K unnecessary allocations/second.

